# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 1: METADATA BLOCK
# ( Identity, Provenance, VCS Exclusion Contracts & System Anchors )
# ==============================================================================
# @project       Tenebris and Lux
# @file          .gitignore
# @layer         Version Control & Workspace Hygiene (Layer 0 Infrastructure)
# @version       0.1.0-dev
# @interface_rev Rev 3
# @date          2026-11-03
# @updated       2026-11-03
# @author        CreativeWorkzStudio LLC / ProfessorSeanEX
# @repository    https://github.com/Novaking34/tenebris-lux
# @system        Git Version Control Invariant Exclusion Engine
# @role          Workspace Boundary Guard & Clean Tree Governance Manifest
# @invariants    1. Zero binary tracking: No machine-generated objects.
#                2. Zero CMake cache leakage: Toolchain paths stay local.
#                3. Zero telemetry leakage: Diagnostic runtime logs stay out.
#                4. Zero user-environment leakage: IDE & OS caches stay out.
#                5. Strict 80-column line width discipline across all lines.
#
# PURPOSE & ARCHITECTURAL ROLE:
#   Repository version control exclusion manifest and root hygiene guard.
#   Guarantees that intermediate build artifacts, machine-specific binaries,
#   IDE workspace states, diagnostic dumps, and OS cache detritus never
#   pollute the Git history or corrupt cross-platform verification trees.
#
# PEDAGOGICAL MISSION & THE BATON-PASSING LIFECYCLE:
#   This file models the Universal 5-Block Lifecycle Protocol:
#   - Block 1 (Metadata): Anchors identity, provenance, and hygiene contracts.
#   - Block 2 (Opening/Objects): Declares all machine binary artifacts.
#   - Block 3 (Body/Procedure): Traverses the build toolchain pipeline.
#   - Block 4 (Audit/Telemetry): Filters forensic dumps, logs, and scratchpads.
#   - Block 5 (Closing/Teardown): Seals against OS and editor state.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING / COMPILED BINARIES BLOCK
# ( The Functional Objects: Declaring Machine Artifacts Prior to Execution )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.binaries
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 2.1: INTERMEDIATE OBJECT FILES & STATIC ARCHIVES ]
# Mission: Insulate the repository from platform-dependent compiler objects.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Intermediate compiler object files (ELF, Mach-O, PE/COFF)
*.o
*.obj

# Static library archives (C11 utility and engine static archives)
*.a
*.lib

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 2.2: DYNAMIC LIBRARIES & SHARED MODULES ]
# Mission: Guard against compiled dynamic linkages and runtime shared libraries.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dynamic shared objects and dynamic link libraries
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 2.3: NATIVE EXECUTABLES & STAGING OUTPUTS ]
# Mission: Prevent compiled binary executables from entering version control.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Native machine executables and bundles
*.exe
*.out
*.app
tenebris-lux

# Build distribution output staging directories
/bin/
out/
dist/

# Rust developer toolchain compilation outputs (tools/Cargo.toml)
target/
tools/target/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY / BUILD SYSTEM PROCEDURAL PIPELINE BLOCK
# ( The Procedural Logic: Build System Lifecycles Passing the Baton )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.cmake
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 3.1: CMAKE BUILD DIRECTORIES & GENERATED CACHES ]
# Mission: Isolate out-of-source CMake build trees and host-specific toolchains.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Primary out-of-source CMake build directories
build/
build-*/

# In-source CMake cache files and generated build manifests
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeScripts/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# CTest test driver files and testing reports
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/

# Compiler commands database (exported for local clangd / LSP engines)
compile_commands.json

# CMake installation manifests and external dependency caches
install_manifest.txt
_deps/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 3.2: DOCUMENTATION TOOLCHAIN TEMPORARY ARTIFACTS ]
# Mission: Prevent transient docbook and asciidoctor compile intermediates.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Asciidoctor and PDF compilation scratch files
*.tmp
*.temp
.asciidoctor/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: AUDIT PROCEDURES, LOGS & TELEMETRY BLOCK
# ( The Audit Track: Forensic Telemetry, Diagnostics & Scratch Verification )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.telemetry
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 4.1: DIAGNOSTIC LOGS & TELEMETRY ROTATION DUMPS ]
# Mission: Filter diagnostic logs, rotation histories, and runtime crash traces.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Engine diagnostic runtime traces and rotation files
*.log
*.log.*
*.audit
*.telemetry

# Dedicated telemetry and log archives
logs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 4.2: SCRATCHPADS & TEST HARNESS WORKING DIRECTORIES ]
# Mission: Isolate non-canonical experimental scripts and test outputs.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Temporary scratchpads, experiment scripts, and sandbox directories
scratch/
test_output/
debug_dumps/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 5: CLOSING / WORKSPACES & OS TEARDOWN BLOCK
# ( The Closing Handshake: Sealing Against IDE, Editor & OS State Detritus )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.workspaces
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.1: IDE WORKSPACES & LANGUAGE SERVER CACHES ]
# Mission: Protect repository hygiene from developer-specific editor state.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IDE workspace folders and metadata
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/

# Vim / Emacs swap buffers, lockfiles, and backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.2: OPERATING SYSTEM FILESYSTEM DETRITUS ]
# Mission: Guard against platform-specific desktop indexes and thumbnail stores.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# macOS metadata and desktop index files
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows desktop databases and thumbnail caches
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Linux filesystem metadata
.directory

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.3: PACKAGE MANAGERS & PATCH ARTIFACTS ]
# Mission: Prevent local package caches and patch rejects from entering tree.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local package manager directories and logs
node_modules/
.npm/
.gem/

# Git patch application temporary and reject files
*.patch
*.orig
*.rej

# End of .gitignore
